From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Benjamin Kelenyi <benjamin@wendy.sh>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: qrb2210-arduino-imola: keep the ADSP remote
 heap out of the page allocator

agatti.dtsi declares the ADSP FastRPC remote heap as a reusable CMA pool.
The ADSP has no IOMMU, so fastrpc hands the whole region to the DSP through
the hypervisor at probe, while the page allocator keeps lending the pool's
pages to movable allocations. Under memory pressure Linux then touches
DSP-owned memory and the board resets.

Declare the heap no-map, as monaco.dtsi and lemans.dtsi do.

Upstream-Status: Submitted [https://lore.kernel.org/linux-arm-msm/20261001085247.1897991-1-benjamin@wendy.sh/]
Signed-off-by: Benjamin Kelenyi <benjamin@wendy.sh>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qrb2210-arduino-imola.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qrb2210-arduino-imola.dts
@@ -222,6 +222,15 @@
 	};
 };
 
+/*
+ * The ADSP has no IOMMU, so fastrpc hands its whole remote heap to the DSP
+ * through the hypervisor; a reusable pool would also be lent to Linux.
+ */
+&adsp_rpc_remote_heap_mem {
+	/delete-property/ reusable;
+	no-map;
+};
+
 &gpi_dma0 {
 	status = "okay";
 };
